## Hints for Future Agents
Closure results describe the first node with local object constraints, not the last reference target. A locally closed target may itself reference an unconstrained schema; do not follow past its closure when resolving an alias. Cache intermediate untyped aliases as well as object-typed aliases. Preserve full internal JSON Pointer paths and truncate only diagnostic rendering. Do not rely on an async timeout alone to detect CPU starvation on a single-thread runtime. Test commands used Homebrew Rust 1.99.0, while lint and formatting used the pinned 1.96.1 toolchain through its bin directory.

## Codebase Discoveries
Schema definition counts have no separate node cap, so a 16,000-alias chain with short names fits the existing character budget. Responses performs strict validation during conversion and again through Chat validation. The fix removes repeated suffix traversal within each pass without changing those validation boundaries or schema acceptance.

